{"name":"Meadowood","hex":"#9da28e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Meadowood, Pennsylvania","blocks":[{"text":"Meadowood is a census-designated place (CDP) in Butler County, Pennsylvania, United States. The population was 2,693 at the 2010 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Map_of_Meadowood%2C_Butler_County%2C_Pennsylvania_Highlighted.png/330px-Map_of_Meadowood%2C_Butler_County%2C_Pennsylvania_Highlighted.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meadowood%2C_Pennsylvania","wikidata":"Q1183604"},{"title":"Meadowood Mall","blocks":[{"text":"Meadowood Mall is a one-level, 901,357-square-foot (83,738.8 m2) super-regional mall in Reno, Nevada, managed by Simon Property Group, which owns 50% of it. Meadowood Mall contains 125 retailers and restaurants and it is anchored by Macy's Women, Macy's Men/Home, JCPenney, Round One Entertainment, and Dick's Sporting Goods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Meadowood_Mall%2C_Reno%2C_Nevada_%2818201371195%29.jpg/330px-Meadowood_Mall%2C_Reno%2C_Nevada_%2818201371195%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meadowood_Mall","wikidata":"Q3303775"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Meadowood_Mall_Construction_2013.jpg/500px-Meadowood_Mall_Construction_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Meadowood_Mall_Construction_2013.jpg/1280px-Meadowood_Mall_Construction_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Meadowood_Mall_Construction_2013.jpg/500px-Meadowood_Mall_Construction_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content